course: dictionary
lesson: 7281
title: A tiny hole, a big picture
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pinhole is a very small hole, like one made by a pin. Light can pass through it, but only a thin beam at a time.
explain: A pinhole camera is a simple camera made from a box with a tiny hole and no lens. Light travels in straight lines through the hole, so the picture on the inside of the box comes out upside down.
explain: «Pinhole» can also describe a thing, as in «pinhole camera» or «pinhole viewer». A pinhole viewer lets you watch the Sun safely during an eclipse, without looking straight at it.
fact: A pinhole is a very small hole, like one made by a pin.
fact: A pinhole camera has no lens, just a box with a tiny hole.
fact: Light travels in straight lines, so the picture inside a pinhole camera is upside down.
fact: «An eclipse of the Sun is watched only with special eclipse glasses or a pinhole projector.»
fact: Never look straight at the Sun during an eclipse. Even a sliver can burn the retina, the seeing layer at the back of the eye, and it does not hurt while it happens.
exercise: What is a pinhole? | A kind of glass lens | *A very small hole, like one made by a pin | A large window in a wall | A tube for holding a pencil
exercise: A pinhole camera has no lens. What makes its picture? | A glass lens that bends the light | Sound waves from the room | A battery and a small screen | *Light travelling in straight lines through a tiny hole
exercise: «Never look at a solar eclipse with bare eyes or ordinary sunglasses.» What should you use instead? | A mirror placed on the ground | *Proper eclipse glasses or a pinhole projector | Ordinary sunglasses, but darker | Your bare eyes, but for a shorter time
test: In a pinhole camera, why does the picture appear upside down? | *Light travels in straight lines, so the top of the scene lands at the bottom | The lens flips the picture | The box was turned the wrong way up | Sound makes the picture turn over
test: Why is looking at the Sun during an eclipse unsafe even when it does not hurt? | Because the Sun gets hotter during an eclipse | *Because even a sliver can burn the retina without you feeling it | Because the sky goes dark for hours | Because your eyes get tired quickly
exam: Which of these is the safe way to watch a solar eclipse? | *A pinhole viewer or proper eclipse glasses | Bare eyes for just one second | Looking straight at it through a telescope | Ordinary sunglasses held up to the sky
